From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:42:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 207/207] Meridian: fewer browser crashes, and a reopen after
 one

- LoadWaiter finished (and DeleteSoon'ed itself) more than once: a double free
  in the browser process (crash 20.11 19:04 in 0.6.13, DeleteHelper::DoDelete
  on freed memory). FileInputSetter finishes once too.
- Detaching an embedded tab called ReportBadMessage outside a mojo dispatch
  (SurfaceEmbedConnector::Detach -> FrameNodeImpl::SetViewportIntersection):
  a crash of the whole browser; now ignored.
- macOS: a crash watcher reopens Meridian after a crash of the browser
  process (not after a clean quit, not twice in 2 minutes, not under tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
